# Stage 2 for stars, quick: 30 synthetic stars with measured radial velocities, each with 10 named clusters (its source
# cluster first when it was planted), 1000 clones, dt 0.05 Myr. The clusters= lists skip the prefilter, so the work is
# exact: 300 pairs x 1000 clones x about 700 steps (see the summary make_bench_data.py prints).
# Why: the same loop as pulsar.wu, but with many small pairs and with known radial velocities, as in stage 2: the GPU
# app's batches (262,144 clones) then hold many pairs, each with its own host draw, and the CPU app takes its clusters=
# path (in_list). It is also a pair-mode profile whose size does not depend on how many clusters the prefilter passes.
# The clone count of a real stage-2 task is not in this repository; 1000 is the pulsar figure.
# Expected on an Apple M1: 20-60 s. Expected, not measured.
header PHYGAS 1 pair 1000 0.05
clusters 4087
targets 30
kind S
listed 10
seed 1
